<!-- NOTE: Before anyone signs in - how the node sees this connection, and its state. Shown above every
     arriving screen; "/system" decides both (Home App Scope, R1). -->
<div class="home-arrive-bar" id="arrive_bar" hidden>
   <span class="home-pill" id="security_pill" title="How the node sees this connection - from /system" hidden></span>
   <span class="home-pill" id="state_pill" hidden></span>
</div>

<!-- NOTE: The shared sign in ("signin.js") is built here. -->
<div id="signin_host"></div>

<div class="chat-signin" id="checking_view">
   <div class="chat-signin-form">
      <p class="chat-signin-lede" role="status">Looking for the node&hellip;</p>
   </div>
</div>

<div class="chat-signin" id="unreachable_view" hidden>
   <div class="chat-signin-form">
      <div class="chat-brand">
         <span class="chat-logo"></span>
         <span class="chat-wordmark">CIYAM</span>
         <span class="chat-brand-note">home</span>
      </div>

      <h2 tabindex="-1">The node did not answer</h2>
      <p class="chat-signin-lede">This address did not answer as a CIYAM node. It may be starting up, or the
       connection may be down.</p>

      <div class="chat-signin-actions">
         <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="unreachable_retry">Try again</button>
      </div>
   </div>
</div>

<!-- NOTE: Setting up a new node from here (Damon and Ian, 2026-10-12 - "Home App Scope", Setting up a new node). One card,
     a view at a time: before you start, the person's randomness (bubbles - never their own words: Ian, 2026-10-12, the
     twelfth word is a checksum and people choose poor words; typing words is for restoring), the master password,
     the twelve words, checking them, done - and, when something goes wrong, carrying on after a reload or a node already
     being set up. Nothing is sent before the words; between the node's two set up requests the page must finish. -->
<div class="chat-signin" id="setup_view" hidden>
   <div class="chat-signin-form home-setup">
      <div class="chat-brand">
         <span class="chat-logo"></span>
         <span class="chat-wordmark">CIYAM</span>
         <span class="chat-brand-note">home</span>
      </div>

      <div class="home-setup-progress" id="setup_progress" hidden>
         <span class="home-note" id="setup_step"></span>
         <span class="home-setup-bars" aria-hidden="true">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span>
         </span>
      </div>

      <section id="setup_intro">
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Set up this node</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">It has no identity yet, so nobody can sign in. Is it a new node, or does it take the place
          of one you had?</p>
         <!-- NOTE: New, or recover (Damon, 2026-10-13) - a machine taking the place of a node lost, failed or moved becomes
              that node again from its twelve words: the shared recovery, worded for it ("recover_show( { fresh } )"). -->
         <fieldset class="home-setup-kinds">
            <legend class="home-visually-hidden">New, or recover</legend>
            <label class="home-setup-kind">
               <input type="radio" name="setup_kind" value="new" id="setup_kind_new" checked>
               <span><b>A new node</b><span>New twelve words, a master password and admin's PIN - a few minutes.</span></span>
            </label>
            <label class="home-setup-kind">
               <input type="radio" name="setup_kind" value="recover" id="setup_kind_recover">
               <span><b>Recover a node from its twelve words</b><span>This machine takes the place of one that was lost,
                failed or moved. With its words it becomes that node again - and the nodes holding its backups know it.</span></span>
            </label>
         </fieldset>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede" id="setup_gives_lede">Setting it up gives it:</p>
         <ol class="home-setup-gives" id="setup_gives">
            <li><b>Twelve words</b> that can always restore it - written down on paper and kept safe</li>
            <li><b>A master password</b> - admin's password, and what unlocks the node after a restart</li>
            <li><b>Admin's PIN</b>, to sign in and add the people who use it</li>
         </ol>
         <div class="recover-warning"><b>Before it's on the internet.</b> Whoever sets a node up first owns it. Do this while
          only you can reach it - on your own network, before it's connected to the internet.</div>
         <p class="recover-note" id="setup_tip"><b>Finish in this tab.</b> Have paper and a pen ready. Once the words are made, the
          node waits for this page to finish.</p>
         <p class="recover-note" id="setup_tip_recover" hidden><b>Have its twelve words to hand</b> - the paper you wrote them on
          when it was first set up. Its old master password isn't needed: you'll choose a new one.</p>
         <div class="chat-signin-actions">
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_start">Start setting up</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_random" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Add your own randomness</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">Pop twelve bubbles as they rise. Exactly when and where you catch each one is mixed with
          the node's own suggestion, so neither alone decides your twelve words.</p>
         <div class="home-bubbles" id="setup_bubbles" role="group" aria-label="Bubbles to pop"></div>
         <div class="home-setup-count">
            <span id="setup_popped">0 of 12 popped</span>
            <span>The browser adds its own randomness too</span>
         </div>
         <div class="home-setup-meter" aria-hidden="true"><span id="setup_popped_bar"></span></div>
         <div class="home-setup-actions">
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_random_next" disabled>Next</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_password" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Choose the master password</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">It's admin's password, and it unlocks the node after a restart. Make it long - a few
          unrelated words is easy to remember and hard to guess.</p>
         <label class="chat-label" for="setup_password_new">Master password</label>
         <input type="password" class="chat-field" id="setup_password_new" autocomplete="new-password">
         <div class="chat-strength" id="setup_strength" hidden>
            <div class="chat-strength-track"><div class="chat-strength-bar"></div></div>
            <span class="chat-strength-label" id="setup_strength_label"></span>
         </div>
         <label class="chat-label" for="setup_password_confirm">Type it again</label>
         <input type="password" class="chat-field" id="setup_password_confirm" autocomplete="new-password">
         <div class="recover-warning" id="setup_http_warning" hidden><b>Over plain HTTP.</b> The connection isn't encrypted. The
          password is hashed in this browser before it's sent, but the randomness your words come from isn't - use your own
          network only.</div>
         <p class="recover-note" id="setup_password_note">Next, the node makes your words - from here, finish in this tab.
          Nothing has been sent to the node yet.</p>
         <div class="chat-error-text signin-error" id="setup_password_error" role="alert"></div>
         <div class="recover-status" id="setup_password_status" role="status"></div>
         <div class="home-setup-actions">
            <button type="button" class="home-link-button" id="setup_password_back">&larr; Back</button>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_make_words">Make my twelve words</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_words" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Write down your twelve words</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">On paper, in order. They can restore the node if everything else is lost - and anyone who
          has them can take it over.</p>
         <ol class="home-setup-words" id="setup_word_list"></ol>
         <div class="recover-warning"><b>Shown only now.</b> Not a screenshot, not a file on this computer, not a photo. The node
          never shows them again, and this page forgets them once the node is set up.</div>
         <p class="recover-note" id="setup_words_note"></p>
         <label class="home-setup-tick">
            <input type="checkbox" id="setup_written">
            <span>I've written all twelve down, in order</span>
         </label>
         <div class="home-setup-actions">
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_words_next" disabled>Check them</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_check" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Check what you wrote</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">From your paper, not from memory: for each word, pick the one you wrote. The words are
          hidden now, and the node is still waiting - there's no hurry.</p>
         <div class="home-setup-check" id="setup_check_rows"></div>
         <div class="home-setup-count">
            <span id="setup_check_count">0 of 12 right</span>
            <span>All twelve, then the node is set up</span>
         </div>
         <div class="home-setup-meter is-good" aria-hidden="true"><span id="setup_check_bar"></span></div>
         <div class="chat-error-text signin-error" id="setup_finish_error" role="alert"></div>
         <div class="recover-status" id="setup_finish_status" role="status"></div>
         <div class="home-setup-actions">
            <button type="button" class="home-link-button" id="setup_check_back">&larr; See the words again</button>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_finish" disabled>Finish setting up</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_done" hidden>
         <span class="home-setup-done" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Your node is set up</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede" id="setup_done_lede">You're signed in as admin. One more thing to write down - admin's PIN.
          It's shown only now; you sign in with it and the master password.</p>
         <div class="chat-error-text signin-error" id="setup_done_error" role="alert" hidden></div>
         <div class="home-setup-pin">
            <span class="chat-label">Admin's PIN</span>
            <span class="recover-mono" id="setup_pin"></span>
         </div>
         <p class="recover-note"><b>Next, in Home:</b> make an unlock key or two, so a restart doesn't need the master password -
          then add the people who'll use the node.</p>
         <label class="home-setup-tick">
            <input type="checkbox" id="setup_pin_written">
            <span>I've written admin's PIN down</span>
         </label>
         <div class="home-setup-actions">
            <span></span>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_continue" disabled>Continue to Home</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_resume" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">Carry on setting up</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">This tab was reloaded after the node started making your words, so it's waiting to be
          finished. For safety the words weren't kept - you'll get new ones.</p>
         <div class="recover-warning"><b>Wrote some words down already?</b> Cross them out - they won't be the node's. Only the
          twelve you check at the end count.</div>
         <div class="chat-signin-actions">
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_resume_go">Carry on</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <section id="setup_elsewhere" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">This node is already being set up</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">Someone has started setting it up - in another tab or browser, or on another device - and
          only they can finish it.</p>
         <div class="chat-error-text signin-error"><b>If it wasn't you,</b> someone else can reach this node. Disconnect it from
          the network now, and set it up again from its terminal.</div>
         <p class="recover-note">If it was you, go back to that tab and finish there. If that tab was closed, the node stops waiting
          for it five minutes after it last heard from it - then <b>Check again</b> starts afresh.</p>
         <div class="chat-signin-actions">
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="setup_retry">Check again</button>
         </div>
      </section>

      <!-- NOTE: The node waits five minutes from its last word with this tab (Ian, 2026-10-12), and the tab keeps it waiting
           while it is open - so this is a tab that slept, or was set aside, for longer. -->
      <section id="setup_expired" hidden>
         <h2 tabindex="-1">The node stopped waiting</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">It waits five minutes at a time, and this tab was away longer - asleep, or set aside - or the
          node restarted, so it let this setup go.</p>
         <div class="recover-warning"><b>Cross out the words you wrote down</b> - they won't be the node's. Starting again gives
          you new ones.</div>
         <div class="chat-signin-actions">
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="setup_again">Start again</button>
         </div>
      </section>
   </div>
</div>

<!-- NOTE: Unlocking needs a session - the unlock key is used on one ("employ_unlock_key( )") - so a locked
     node is signed in to first, then unlocked. Anyone with a key may unlock, not only admin (Ian, 2026-10-03). -->
<div class="chat-signin" id="unlock_view" hidden>
   <div class="home-unlock">
      <form class="chat-signin-form" id="unlock_form" novalidate>
         <div class="chat-brand">
            <span class="chat-logo"></span>
            <span class="chat-wordmark">CIYAM</span>
            <span class="chat-brand-note">home</span>
         </div>

         <h2 tabindex="-1">This node is locked</h2>
         <p class="chat-signin-lede">It restarted, and nothing on it can be used until it is unlocked. Use one of the
          unlock keys you kept.</p>

         <label class="chat-label" for="unlock_key">Unlock key</label>
         <input type="text" id="unlock_key" class="chat-field chat-field--mono" placeholder="XXXXX-xxxxx-XXXXX"
          autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false">
         <div class="signin-hint">Each key works once. Make a new one afterwards, in Unlock keys.</div>

         <div class="chat-error-text" id="unlock_error" role="alert"></div>
         <div class="home-done-text" id="unlock_done" role="status"></div>

         <div class="chat-signin-actions">
            <button type="submit" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="unlock_submit">Unlock</button>
            <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="unlock_sign_out">Sign out</button>
         </div>
      </form>

      <!-- NOTE: The master password is a rescue - for someone on the node's own network with no keys left
           (Ian, 2026-10-03). Over a connection the node sees as unencrypted that is said before it is typed. -->
      <details class="home-rescue" id="rescue_panel">
         <summary>No keys left? Use the master password</summary>

         <form id="rescue_form" novalidate>
            <p class="home-note">The master password unlocks the node like a key, but it is the node's most important
             secret. Only type it on a device on the node's own network - never from outside.</p>

            <div class="home-warning" id="rescue_warning" role="alert" hidden>
               <strong>This connection isn't encrypted.</strong> The node sees it as plain text - only use the password
               if you are on the node's own network.
            </div>

            <label class="chat-label" for="rescue_password">Master password</label>
            <input type="password" id="rescue_password" class="chat-field" autocomplete="off">

            <div class="chat-error-text" id="rescue_error" role="alert"></div>

            <div class="chat-signin-actions">
               <button type="submit" class="chat-btn" id="rescue_submit">Unlock with the password</button>
            </div>
         </form>
      </details>

      <p class="home-note home-unlock-foot">After a restart, chat rooms held only in memory may be gone until the node
       restores them.</p>
   </div>
</div>

<!-- NOTE: Signed in, the node ready - the shell (build step 4): a side menu of apps and, for admin, the node's
     sections, with who is signed in and "Sign out". On a phone the menu is a drawer from the top
     bar, admin's sections are chips beneath it, and the apps are a bar along the bottom. The apps other than
     Home open in this tab on its session, as the switcher opens them - a new tab with ctrl or cmd and click
     (2026-10-09). The rail's items are built by "home.js". -->
<div class="home-app" id="app_view" hidden>
   <nav class="home-rail" id="home_rail" aria-label="Home">
      <!-- NOTE: The app switcher - the CIYAM mark and "Home", as at the top of every app ("apps.js", 2026-10-08). -->
      <div class="home-rail-brand" id="apps_host"></div>

      <div class="home-rail-group">
         <span class="home-rail-heading">Go to</span>
         <div id="rail_apps"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="home-rail-group" id="rail_node" hidden>
         <span class="home-rail-heading">Node</span>
         <div id="rail_sections"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="home-rail-spacer"></div>

      <div class="home-rail-user">
         <div class="home-rail-user-row">
            <span class="home-avatar" id="rail_avatar"></span>
            <span class="home-rail-user-text">
               <span class="home-rail-user-name" id="rail_name"></span>
               <span class="home-rail-user-role" id="rail_role"></span>
            </span>
         </div>
         <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="app_sign_out">Sign out</button>
      </div>
   </nav>

   <div class="home-scrim" id="rail_scrim" hidden></div>

   <div class="home-body">
      <header class="home-topbar">
         <button type="button" class="home-menu-button" id="rail_open" aria-label="Open the menu" aria-controls="home_rail"
          aria-expanded="false">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"
             stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h16"></path></svg>
         </button>

         <span class="home-topbar-title">
            <span class="home-topbar-heading" id="top_heading"></span>
            <span class="home-topbar-sub" id="top_sub"></span>
         </span>

         <span class="home-pill" id="app_security_pill" title="How the node sees this connection - from /system" hidden></span>

         <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--mono home-console-toggle" id="console_toggle" hidden>Console</button>

         <span class="home-avatar home-topbar-avatar" id="top_avatar"></span>
      </header>

      <nav class="home-chips" id="home_chips" aria-label="Node" hidden></nav>

      <main class="home-main">
         <!-- NOTE: A member's Home (build step 5) - their apps, what needs them, announcements and their account.
              What it says of the chat is read as the chat reads it ("chat_parse.js"). -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_home" hidden>
            <h1 id="app_greeting"></h1>
            <p class="home-note" id="app_node"></p>

            <!-- NOTE: "My account" first - who you are and your devices, with the accounts page a link away; it was
                 a tile and a card saying much the same (Damon, 2026-10-08). Then the chat. -->
            <div class="home-tiles">
               <section class="home-card home-account-card" aria-labelledby="account_heading">
                  <h2 id="account_heading">My account</h2>
                  <div class="home-rail-user-row">
                     <span class="home-avatar home-avatar--large" id="account_avatar"></span>
                     <span class="home-rail-user-text">
                        <span class="home-rail-user-name" id="account_name"></span>
                        <span class="home-rail-user-role" id="account_role"></span>
                     </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="home-devices">
                     <span class="home-rail-heading">Devices</span>
                     <ul class="home-device-list" id="device_list"></ul>
                     <span class="home-note home-empty" id="device_more"></span>
                     <a href="account.html#mine" class="home-account-link" id="manage_account">Manage my account</a>
                  </div>
               </section>

               <a class="home-tile" href="#" id="tile_chat">
                  <span class="home-tile-top">
                     <span class="home-tile-icon is-chat" id="tile_chat_icon"></span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="home-tile-title">Chat</span>
                  <span class="home-tile-text" id="tile_chat_text">&hellip;</span>
               </a>
            </div>

            <div class="home-column-main">
               <section class="home-card" aria-labelledby="needs_heading">
                  <div class="home-card-head">
                     <h2 id="needs_heading">Needs you</h2>
                     <span class="home-count" id="needs_count" hidden></span>
                  </div>
                  <ul class="home-needs" id="needs_list"></ul>
                  <p class="home-note home-empty" id="needs_empty">Nothing is waiting for you.</p>
               </section>

               <div id="announce_list"></div>
            </div>
         </section>

         <!-- NOTE: Admin's sections (build step 6) - what the web API gives today. Sessions in use and the other
              limits wait on Ian's combined admin request (R2). -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_overview" hidden>
            <div class="home-section-head">
               <span>
                  <h1>Overview</h1>
                  <p class="home-note" id="overview_node"></p>
               </span>
               <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="overview_refresh">Refresh</button>
            </div>

            <div class="home-stats" aria-label="At a glance">
               <div class="home-stat">
                  <span class="home-stat-label">Node</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-value"><span class="home-state-dot"></span><span id="stat_node"></span></span>
                  <span class="home-stat-note" id="stat_node_note">Unlocked</span>
               </div>
               <div class="home-stat">
                  <span class="home-stat-label">Uptime</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-value" id="stat_uptime">&hellip;</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-note">Since the last restart</span>
               </div>
               <div class="home-stat">
                  <span class="home-stat-label">People</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-value"><span id="stat_people">&hellip;</span> <span class="home-stat-unit">active</span></span>
                  <span class="home-stat-note" id="stat_people_note"></span>
               </div>
               <div class="home-stat">
                  <span class="home-stat-label">Sessions</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-value home-stat-value--quiet">Not reported</span>
                  <span class="home-stat-note">Waiting on the node</span>
               </div>
            </div>

            <!-- NOTE: Only what needs you (Damon, 2026-10-12) - each a line with its way to act, from the same rules as Health
                 ("health_issues( )"), so the two always agree; nothing wrong, it says so. The detail is Health's. -->
            <section class="home-attention" id="attention_card" aria-labelledby="attention_heading" hidden>
               <div class="home-attention-head">
                  <h2 id="attention_heading"></h2>
                  <a href="#health" class="home-link" id="attention_all">View Health &rarr;</a>
               </div>
               <ul class="home-attention-list" id="attention_list"></ul>
            </section>
            <p class="home-note" id="attention_rest" hidden>Everything else is OK.
             <a href="#health" class="home-link" id="attention_rest_link">View Health</a></p>

            <section class="home-card home-card--row home-well" id="well_card" aria-labelledby="well_heading" hidden>
               <span class="home-well-tick" aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
               <span class="home-card-body">
                  <h2 id="well_heading">Nothing needs you</h2>
                  <span class="home-note home-empty">Identity, unlock keys, server log and chat rooms are all OK.</span>
               </span>
               <a href="#health" class="chat-btn home-card-action" id="well_health">View Health</a>
            </section>

            <section class="home-quick" aria-labelledby="quick_heading">
               <h2 class="home-rail-heading" id="quick_heading">Quick actions</h2>
               <div class="home-quick-grid" id="quick_actions">
                  <section class="home-card" aria-label="People">
                     <h2>People</h2>
                     <p class="home-note home-empty" id="overview_people"></p>
                     <div class="home-card-actions">
                        <a href="#" class="chat-btn" id="overview_add_person">Add a person</a>
                        <a href="#" class="chat-btn" id="overview_people_link">People</a>
                     </div>
                  </section>
                  <section class="home-card" aria-label="Unlock keys">
                     <h2>Unlock keys</h2>
                     <p class="home-note home-empty" id="overview_keys_line"></p>
                     <div class="home-card-actions">
                        <a href="#keys" class="chat-btn" id="overview_make_key">Make a key</a>
                     </div>
                  </section>
                  <section class="home-card" aria-label="Logs">
                     <h2>Logs</h2>
                     <p class="home-note home-empty">Server and script logs.</p>
                     <div class="home-card-actions">
                        <a href="#logs" class="chat-btn" id="overview_open_logs">View logs</a>
                     </div>
                  </section>
               </div>
            </section>
         </section>

         <!-- NOTE: Health (Damon, 2026-10-12) - every check the node allows a page today, in detail, each card saying whether
              it needs you; its rail item carries how many do. The greyed card at the foot is what Ian's R2 figures would add -
              kept in sight as the gap. -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_health" hidden>
            <div class="home-section-head">
               <span>
                  <h1>Health</h1>
                  <p class="home-note">Checked every minute while open.</p>
               </span>
               <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="health_refresh">Refresh</button>
            </div>

            <div class="home-health-grid">
               <section class="home-card home-health-card" id="health_identity_card" aria-labelledby="health_identity_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="health_identity_heading">Identity and keys</h2>
                     <span class="home-health-pill" id="health_identity_pill"></span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="home-health-line" id="health_secure_line"></p>
                  <p class="home-health-line" id="overview_keys_note"></p>
                  <div class="home-card-actions">
                     <a href="#keys" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="health_make_key">Make a key</a>
                  </div>
               </section>

               <section class="home-card home-health-card" id="health_connection_card" aria-labelledby="connection_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="connection_heading"></h2>
                     <span class="home-health-pill" id="health_connection_pill"></span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="home-mono home-cipher" id="connection_cipher"></span>
                  <p class="home-note home-empty" id="connection_note">As the node sees this browser - behind a proxy, the proxy's.</p>
               </section>

               <section class="home-card home-health-card home-health-wide" id="health_log_card" aria-labelledby="health_log_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="health_log_heading">Server log</h2>
                     <span class="home-health-pill" id="health_log_pill"></span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="home-health-line" id="problems_heading">&hellip;</p>
                  <p class="home-note home-empty" id="problems_latest"></p>
                  <pre class="home-log home-log--short" id="overview_log"></pre>
                  <div class="home-card-actions">
                     <a href="#logs" class="chat-btn" id="problems_show" hidden>Show them</a>
                     <a href="#logs" class="chat-btn" id="health_open_logs">All logs</a>
                  </div>
               </section>

               <section class="home-card home-health-card" id="health_rooms_card" aria-labelledby="health_rooms_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="health_rooms_heading">Chat rooms</h2>
                     <span class="home-health-pill" id="health_rooms_pill"></span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="home-health-line" id="rooms_heading">&hellip;</p>
                  <ul class="home-room-bars" id="rooms_filling"></ul>
                  <p class="home-note home-empty" id="rooms_note">Rooms you're in. Each keeps 9,000 messages, then drops the oldest.</p>
               </section>

               <section class="home-card home-health-card" id="health_node_card" aria-labelledby="health_node_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="health_node_heading">Node</h2>
                     <span class="home-health-pill" id="health_node_pill"></span>
                  </div>
                  <dl class="home-health-facts">
                     <dt>State</dt><dd id="health_state"></dd>
                     <dt>Uptime</dt><dd id="health_uptime"></dd>
                     <dt>Version</dt><dd class="home-mono" id="health_version"></dd>
                     <dt>Kind</dt><dd id="health_kind"></dd>
                  </dl>
               </section>

               <section class="home-health-wide home-health-gap" aria-labelledby="health_gap_heading">
                  <div class="home-health-head">
                     <h2 id="health_gap_heading">Not reported yet</h2>
                     <span class="home-note">Waiting on the node</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="home-health-gap-grid">
                     <span><b>Chat memory</b>Store used, of its limit</span>
                     <span><b>Files area</b>Space used and free</span>
                     <span><b>Sessions in use</b>Of the maximum, and ending one</span>
                     <span><b>Devices</b>Signed in, everyone's</span>
                     <span><b>Updates</b>New version, and installing it</span>
                  </div>
               </section>
            </div>
         </section>

         <!-- NOTE: Unlock keys - made by admin while the node is unlocked, each shown once and used once. The node
              cannot list them, so Home counts the ones made on this browser (the design's known limit). -->
         <!-- NOTE: People - adding, handing over and removing accounts - moved here from the accounts page, which keeps My
              account and Welcome (Damon, 2026-10-11: the node's administration in Home). Its look is "account.css", which
              the accounts page shares. Four views in the one section, as on the accounts page - the list, Add a person,
              the code to hand over and the PIN ready - the last two shown once. -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_people" hidden>
            <div class="account-alert" id="people_alert" role="status" hidden></div>

            <section class="account-section account-section--wide" id="people_section">
               <div class="account-head">
                  <div>
                     <h1 tabindex="-1">People</h1>
                     <p class="account-lede">Everyone with an account on this node. Only you can add people.</p>
                  </div>
                  <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="people_add">Add a person</button>
               </div>

               <div class="account-card account-table-wrap">
                  <table class="account-table">
                     <thead>
                        <tr>
                           <th scope="col">Person</th>
                           <th scope="col">PIN</th>
                           <th scope="col">Status</th>
                           <th scope="col"><span class="account-sr">Actions</span></th>
                        </tr>
                     </thead>
                     <tbody id="people_rows"></tbody>
                  </table>
                  <p class="account-empty" id="people_empty">Loading...</p>
               </div>

               <p class="account-note">PINs are hidden while Home is open - <b>Show</b> one to read it. Codes you've handed out
                but nobody has used yet aren't listed here - the node doesn't keep a list of them.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="account-section" id="add_section" hidden>
               <button type="button" class="account-back" data-people="list">&larr; People</button>

               <form class="account-card account-form" id="add_form" novalidate>
                  <div>
                     <h1 tabindex="-1">Add a person</h1>
                     <p class="account-lede">They choose their own password. You never see it, and neither does the node.</p>
                  </div>

                  <fieldset class="account-choices">
                     <legend class="chat-label">How they'll join</legend>

                     <label class="account-choice">
                        <input type="radio" name="add_how" value="code" checked>
                        <span class="account-choice-text">
                           <span class="account-choice-title">With a code <span class="account-pill account-pill--accent">Recommended</span></span>
                           <span class="account-choice-desc">A one-time code you hand over in person - on screen as a QR code, or read
                            out. They choose their username and password, and the node gives them a PIN.</span>
                        </span>
                     </label>

                     <label class="account-choice">
                        <input type="radio" name="add_how" value="pin">
                        <span class="account-choice-text">
                           <span class="account-choice-title">With a PIN you choose</span>
                           <span class="account-choice-desc">For someone who'd rather not handle a code, such as a household member.
                            You choose the PIN, and can suggest a username.</span>
                        </span>
                     </label>
                  </fieldset>

                  <div class="account-pin-fields" id="add_pin_fields" hidden>
                     <div class="account-grid">
                        <div>
                           <label class="chat-label" for="add_pin">PIN <span class="account-optional">- optional</span></label>
                           <input type="text" id="add_pin" class="chat-field chat-field--mono" inputmode="numeric" maxlength="5" autocomplete="off">
                           <div class="account-hint">5 digits. Leave it empty for a random one.</div>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                           <label class="chat-label" for="add_username">Username <span class="account-optional">- optional</span></label>
                           <input type="text" id="add_username" class="chat-field" maxlength="12" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="none"
                            spellcheck="false">
                           <div class="account-hint">3 to 12 characters: a-z, 0-9 and -</div>
                        </div>
                     </div>

                     <label class="account-check">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="add_suggestion" checked>
                        Only a suggestion - they can choose a different username
                     </label>

                     <div class="account-warning">
                        <b>Hand it over in person.</b>
                        <span>Whoever signs in with this PIN first sets the password.</span>
                     </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="chat-error-text" id="add_error" role="alert"></div>

                  <div class="account-actions-row">
                     <button type="button" class="chat-btn account-btn-tall" data-people="list">Cancel</button>
                     <button type="submit" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="add_submit">Create a code</button>
                  </div>
               </form>
            </section>

            <section class="account-section" id="handover_section" hidden>
               <div class="account-card account-form">
                  <div>
                     <h1 tabindex="-1">Hand this code over in person</h1>
                     <p class="account-lede">It's for one person - it becomes their account when they use it.</p>
                  </div>

                  <div class="account-handover">
                     <div class="account-qr" id="handover_qr" role="img"
                      aria-label="A QR code that opens the accounts page on their phone, with the code filled in"></div>

                     <div class="account-handover-code">
                        <span class="chat-label">The code</span>
                        <span class="chat-mono account-code" id="handover_code"></span>
                        <div>
                           <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="handover_copy">Copy</button>
                        </div>
                        <p class="account-hint">Scanning the QR code opens the accounts page on their phone, with the code filled in.</p>
                     </div>
                  </div>

                  <ol class="account-steps">
                     <li>They scan the QR code - or open <b class="chat-mono" id="handover_url"></b> and type the code</li>
                     <li>They choose a username and a password</li>
                     <li>They write down the PIN they're given</li>
                  </ol>

                  <div class="account-warning">
                     <b>Shown only now.</b>
                     <span>The node can't show this code again. If it's lost before they use it, add them again.</span>
                  </div>

                  <div class="account-actions-row">
                     <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="handover_done" data-people="list">Done</button>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </section>

            <section class="account-section" id="ready_section" hidden>
               <div class="account-card account-form">
                  <div>
                     <h1 tabindex="-1">The PIN is ready</h1>
                     <p class="account-lede">Give it to them in person. They set their password the first time they sign in with it.</p>
                  </div>

                  <div class="account-facts account-facts--row">
                     <div class="account-fact">
                        <span class="chat-label">PIN</span>
                        <span class="chat-mono account-fact-big" id="ready_pin"></span>
                     </div>
                     <div class="account-fact">
                        <span class="chat-label">Username</span>
                        <span class="account-fact-name" id="ready_username"></span>
                        <span class="account-hint" id="ready_username_note"></span>
                     </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="account-warning">
                     <b>Until they sign in,</b>
                     <span>anyone with this PIN can set the password. It shows in People as "Not yet claimed" until then.
                      They set it up at <b class="chat-mono" id="ready_url"></b>, under "I have a PIN".</span>
                  </div>

                  <div class="account-actions-row">
                     <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="ready_done" data-people="list">Done</button>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </section>

            <template id="tpl_person">
               <tr>
                  <td>
                     <div class="account-who">
                        <span class="account-avatar"></span>
                        <div>
                           <div class="account-name"></div>
                           <div class="account-sub"></div>
                        </div>
                     </div>
                  </td>
                  <td>
                     <span class="chat-mono account-pin"></span>
                     <button type="button" class="account-pin-show">Show</button>
                  </td>
                  <td><span class="account-pill"></span></td>
                  <td class="account-row-actions">
                     <span class="account-you" hidden>You</span>
                     <button type="button" class="chat-btn account-remove">Remove</button>
                     <div class="account-confirm" hidden>
                        <span class="account-confirm-text"></span>
                        <button type="button" class="account-btn-danger account-confirm-yes">Remove for good</button>
                        <button type="button" class="chat-btn account-confirm-no">Keep</button>
                     </div>
                  </td>
               </tr>
            </template>
         </section>

         <section class="home-section" id="section_keys" hidden>
            <h1>Unlock keys</h1>
            <p class="home-note">A key unlocks the node after a restart without the master password - from anywhere, by
             anyone who has it. Each works once. Keep a few somewhere safe: a password manager, or written down.</p>

            <section class="home-card home-keys-card">
               <p class="home-note home-empty" id="keys_note"></p>
               <div class="home-card-actions">
                  <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="key_make">Make a key</button>
               </div>
               <div class="chat-error-text" id="key_error" role="alert"></div>

               <div class="home-new-key" id="key_shown" hidden>
                  <span class="home-rail-heading">Your new key - shown once</span>
                  <div class="home-new-key-row">
                     <span class="home-key-qr" id="key_qr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                     <span class="home-new-key-text">
                        <span class="home-key" id="key_text"></span>
                        <span class="home-note home-empty">Store it now - it cannot be shown again. A phone can scan the
                         code into a password manager.</span>
                        <span class="home-card-actions">
                           <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="key_copy">Copy</button>
                           <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="key_stored">I've stored it</button>
                        </span>
                     </span>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </section>
         </section>

         <!-- NOTE: Alerts (Damon, 2026-10-12 - "Home App Scope", Notifications) - ntfy on a phone. Three kinds: the node's
              notices for everyone, admin's own, and each person's - every one sent to that person's own topic, never a shared
              one. Admin's is the node's own topic, readable today only on a development node; each person's waits on Ian. -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_alerts" hidden>
            <h1>Alerts</h1>
            <p class="home-note">Notifications on a phone, through the ntfy app - the node's alerts for admin now, and later
             each person's own.</p>

            <section class="home-card" aria-labelledby="alerts_server_heading">
               <h2 id="alerts_server_heading">ntfy server</h2>
               <p class="home-note home-empty">Where the phones reach ntfy - kept in this browser.</p>
               <form class="home-alerts-server" id="alerts_server_form" novalidate>
                  <label class="home-visually-hidden" for="alerts_server">ntfy server address</label>
                  <input type="url" class="chat-field chat-field--mono" id="alerts_server" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
                  <button type="submit" class="chat-btn">Save</button>
               </form>
               <div class="chat-error-text" id="alerts_server_error" role="alert"></div>
            </section>

            <section class="home-card" aria-labelledby="alerts_admin_heading">
               <div class="home-health-head">
                  <h2 id="alerts_admin_heading">Node admin alerts</h2>
                  <span class="home-health-pill" id="alerts_admin_pill"></span>
               </div>
               <p class="home-health-line" id="alerts_admin_line"></p>
               <div class="home-new-key-row" id="alerts_subscribe" hidden>
                  <span class="home-key-qr" id="alerts_qr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="home-new-key-text">
                     <span class="home-rail-heading">Topic</span>
                     <span class="home-key home-key--topic" id="alerts_topic"></span>
                     <span class="home-alerts-codes" role="group" aria-label="What the code opens">
                        <button type="button" class="chat-btn is-current" id="alerts_code_app" aria-pressed="true">For the ntfy app</button>
                        <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="alerts_code_web" aria-pressed="false">For an iPhone</button>
                     </span>
                     <span class="home-note home-empty" id="alerts_code_note"></span>
                     <span class="home-card-actions">
                        <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="alerts_copy">Copy topic</button>
                        <button type="button" class="chat-btn chat-btn--primary" id="alerts_test">Send a test alert</button>
                     </span>
                     <span class="home-note" id="alerts_test_status" role="status"></span>
                  </span>
               </div>
               <p class="home-note home-empty" id="alerts_admin_today" hidden>Today the node sends here only what it is asked to,
                like the test. Its own alerts - restarted, waiting to be unlocked, an error, a room filling - are still to
                come from the node.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="home-health-gap" aria-labelledby="alerts_mine_heading">
               <div class="home-health-head">
                  <h2 id="alerts_mine_heading">My notifications</h2>
                  <span class="home-note">Waiting on the node</span>
               </div>
               <p class="home-alerts-gap-text">Each person's own topic: the node's notices for everyone - down, back up, planned
                downtime - and their own direct messages and invitations, never their words. Coming once the node sends them.</p>
            </section>
         </section>

         <!-- NOTE: The node's logs, read only - admin's (Ian, 2026-10-03). The newest at the end, as in the file. -->
         <section class="home-section" id="section_logs" hidden>
            <div class="home-section-head">
               <h1>Logs</h1>
               <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="logs_refresh">Refresh</button>
            </div>

            <div class="home-log-bar">
               <div class="home-log-tabs" id="log_tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Logs"></div>
               <input type="search" class="chat-field home-log-filter" id="log_filter" placeholder="Filter" aria-label="Filter the log">
               <select class="chat-field home-log-count" id="log_count" aria-label="How many lines">
                  <option value="100">Last 100 lines</option>
                  <option value="200" selected>Last 200 lines</option>
                  <option value="1000">Last 1000 lines</option>
                  <option value="0">Every line</option>
               </select>
            </div>
            <!-- NOTE: The Overview's "Show them" - only the lines it counted (2026-10-12). -->
            <div class="home-log-only" id="log_problems_only" hidden>
               <span id="log_problems_label"></span>
               <button type="button" class="chat-btn" id="log_problems_clear">Show the whole log</button>
            </div>
            <p class="home-note" id="log_status" role="status"></p>
            <pre class="home-log" id="log_lines"></pre>
         </section>
      </main>

      <nav class="home-bottombar" id="home_bottombar" aria-label="Go to"></nav>
   </div>
</div>

<!-- NOTE: The console drawer - as in the chat and the accounts page, handed Home's session (Damon, 2026-10-08). -->
<div id="console_drawer" class="chat-console" hidden>
   <div class="chat-console-bar">
      <span class="chat-console-label">Console</span>
      <span class="chat-console-session">
         <span class="chat-dot"></span>
         <span id="console_session"></span>
      </span>
      <button type="button" class="chat-console-close" id="console_popout"
       aria-label="Open the console in its own window" title="Open in its own window">&#8599;</button>
      <button type="button" class="chat-console-close" id="console_close" aria-label="Close console">&times;</button>
   </div>
</div>
